<p>Dear Eden,</p>
<p>Thank you again for the pilot reels that we ordered in August. Our tests=
 with the assembled panels went well, and the LEDs are very bright, except =
for the yellow (YY0402YE-NN1S0-T1AR4), which is noticeably dimmer than the =
others. We therefore want to do
 one more round of testing before we prepare the larger batch order. I am l=
ooking into brighter parts and would like to order the following as soon as=
 possible:</p>
<p>- YY0402YE-RN3S0-T1AR4 (yellow): 3,000 pcs<br>
- YY0402RE-RN3S0-T1AR4 (red): 3,000 pcs</p>
<p>Shipped to JLCPCB, as before. If your reels hold more (for example 5,000=
 pcs), one full reel of each is fine.</p>
<p>Could you please:</p>
<p>1. Confirm that the RN3S0 parts are the brighter version: the datasheet =
gives 250-620 mcd at 20 mA for YE-RN3S0, against 70-175 mcd for YE-NN3S0 an=
d 20-48 mcd at 5 mA for the YE-NN1S0 we bought.<br>
2. Confirm that both parts are in stock, with the brightest intensity bins =
you have, and send a proforma invoice so we can issue the PO right away.<br=
>
3. Clarify the polarity. The datasheet lists the RN parts as &quot;Reverse&=
quot;. Is the cathode mark at the opposite end compared with the NN parts w=
e bought, and is the package otherwise the same? A photo or drawing of the =
marking and the tape orientation would be
 very helpful.<br>
4. As last time, send the label information (bin codes) before shipment.</p=
>
<p>Thank you very much!</p>
<p>Best regards,</p>
<p><br>
Michael</p>
